	<key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island reads what is playing in Music and Spotify, controls playback from the notch, and sends the iMessage replies you type.</string>
	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island listens to what your Mac is playing so the notch waveform moves with the music. Nothing is recorded or saved.</string>
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island shows when AirPods and other Bluetooth devices connect, with their battery levels.</string>
	<key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island shows your events in the notch and reminds you before meetings.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island shows your front camera as a mirror in the notch when you open the Mirror tab. Nothing is recorded.</string>
	<key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island watches your Downloads folder to show download progress in the notch. It only looks at file names and sizes.</string>
	<key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>P Island turns speech in your audio and video files into text, only when you ask.</string>
